2023: \begin{proposition}[Minimal bad-record witness for command-run escalation]
2024: \label{prop:publication-safety-minimal-bad-record-witness}
2025: In the operational interface of
2026: Definition~\ref{def:operational-acceptance-interface}, let $r$ be a submitted
2027: claim record whose claim-kind set is \{route\}, whose evidence level is declared
2028: to be command-run, and whose boundary field contains no command-run tuple
2029: $(\text{command},\text{source state},\text{environment},\text{exit code},
2030: \text{log path})$.  Suppose all other route coordinates of $r$ are filled:
2031: there is an evidence pointer, a human-promotion marker at the declared boundary,
2032: and pass rows for the promotion, overlap, and submission-state gates.  Then the
2033: schema verifier rejects $r$, and the inclusion-minimal bad subrecord is exactly
2034: the pair consisting of the evidence-level declaration ``command-run'' and the
2035: boundary field missing the five command-run coordinates.  In particular, adding
2036: more prose, advisory scores, route history, or path-verified evidence surfaces
2037: cannot repair the rejected stronger reading unless the missing command-run tuple
2038: is added as a finite coordinate.
2039: \end{proposition}
2040: 
2041: \begin{proof}
2042: For a route claim, the dispatch table in
2043: Definition~\ref{def:operational-acceptance-interface} requires the promotion,
2044: overlap, and submission-state gates.  By hypothesis those pass rows and the
2045: route-boundary marker are already present, so clauses A1--A4 and A6 of
2046: Definition~\ref{def:certificate-schema-acceptance-table} have no missing route,
2047: evidence-surface, gate-coverage, or promotion coordinate to report.  The only
2048: remaining clause that reads the declared evidence level is the command-run part
2049: of the boundary condition: at command-run strength the boundary field must
2050: contain the command, immutable source state, environment, exit code, and log
2051: path.  These five fields are absent by hypothesis, so the verifier rejects.
2052: 
2053: The bad subrecord is inclusion-minimal.  If the evidence-level declaration is
2054: removed, the command-run boundary obligation is no longer triggered by the
2055: record.  If the boundary field is replaced by one containing the five command-run
2056: coordinates, the displayed obstruction disappears and the record must be tested
2057: against the remaining clauses, which were assumed filled.  Deleting any unrelated
2058: prose, advisory score, route-history note, or path-verified surface does not add
2059: the missing five fields and therefore cannot change the failed command-run
2060: clause.  Thus the rejected stronger reading is witnessed by a finite bad record,
2061: not by a semantic judgment about the surrounding pipeline.  This is the concrete
2062: negative instance used by Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface},
2063: Proposition~\ref{prop:publication-safety-maximality}, and
2064: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-extension-budget-normal-form} when a path-verified route
2065: or submission row is silently upgraded to command-run strength.
2066: \end{proof}